  "id": "MK-080",
  "blind_answer": "A",
  "key": "C",
  "agree": false,
  "explanation_ok": false,
  "issue": "No correct choice. Side = 40/4 = 10 yd, area = 100 sq yd = 900 sq ft. Key C (300 sq ft) is wrong (uses 3 sq ft per sq yd), and the explanation itself says none of the choices match, so it contradicts the keyed answer. Fix the choices: e.g. change A to \"100 square yards\" (or C to \"900 square feet\") and rekey.",
  "suggested_explanation": "The perimeter of a square is 4 times one side, so each side is 40 / 4 = 10 yards. The area of a square is s^2 = 10 yd x 10 yd = 100 square yards. (In square feet: 1 square yard = 3 ft x 3 ft = 9 square feet, so 100 x 9 = 900 square feet. A common mistake is to multiply by 3 instead of 9, which gives 300.) The area is 100 square yards. [Requires a choice reading 100 square yards (or 900 square feet) to be added and keyed.]"
 },
